   "subject": "Re: how to use only data from another package",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You know, I considered that.  That solution reminds of how they required me to add code like this in every file where I use ggplot2: <div><br></div><div><div>(base::getRversion() &gt;= &quot;2.15.1&quot;) {<br>\r\n</div><div>  utils::globalVariables(c(...))</div><div>}</div></div><div><br></div><div>We had some back and forth about this, but they insisted I add it.  (See <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/9439256/how-can-i-handle-r-cmd-check-no-visible-binding-for-global-variable-notes-when\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/9439256/how-can-i-handle-r-cmd-check-no-visible-binding-for-global-variable-notes-when&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792490087289000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1AACwXXHzbufsSigZP-cNG\">this</a> stackoverflow for a larger discussion about this problem).  </div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>Overall, I feel that adding code to my project to satisfy &quot;notes&quot; from an automated program lowers the quality of my project.  But if enough users mention the problem that my dependency declaration causes I&#39;ll consider doing this.</div>\r\n<div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Feb 11, 2014 at 6:21 AM, Timothy Bates <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">timothy...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">create a function called <div><br></div><div><div>cran_satisfier &lt;- function(x) {maps::something() }</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>??</div><div><div><br></div><br>On Sunday, February 9, 2014 7:59:29 PM UTC-6, Hadley Wickham wrote:</div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div>To the best of my knowledge I don&#39;t think there is a good solution. I think the check warming you got is spurious (and occurs in other places) but I&#39;m not sure how hard it will be to persuade cran on that. <div>\r\n<br>\r\n</div></div><div>Hadley <div><div><br><br>On Friday, February 7, 2014,  &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">arila...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">I just released my <a href=\"http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/choroplethr/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/choroplethr/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792490087289000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3wen5fXyWExEnsUSW8av_t\">package</a> on cran and users are reporting a problem that I am now able to reproduce.  It has to do with Imports vs. Suggets vs. Depends.  You can see my DESCRIPTION file <a href=\"https://github.com/trulia/choroplethr/blob/master/DESCRIPTION\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/trulia/choroplethr/blob/master/DESCRIPTION&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792490087289000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3XR85bcYhkv8BAGoscNBhg\">here</a>, and I&#39;ll reproduce the important parts below<div>\r\n\r\n<br></div><div><pre><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\">Imports:</div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\">\r\n\r\n    ggplot2,</div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\">Suggests:<br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\">\r\n\r\n    maps,<br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\">    zipcode</div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\">\r\n\r\n<br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;white-space:normal\">The reason that I put maps and zipcode in Suggets and not Imports is because R CMD generates this NOTE which prevented acceptance by CRAN:</span><br>\r\n\r\n</div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;padding-left:10px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:normal;white-space:normal\"><br>\r\n\r\n</span></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">* checking dependencies in R code ... NOTE</span></font></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\">\r\n\r\n<font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">Namespaces in Imports field not imported from:</span></font></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">  ‘maps’ ‘zipcode’</span></font></div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">  All declared Imports should be used.</span></font></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">See the information on DESCRIPTION files in the chapter ‘Creating R</span></font></div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">packages’ of the ‘Writing R Extensions’ manual.</span></font></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><br>\r\n\r\n</span></font></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">While it&#39;s true that my NAMESPACE file does not mention these packages, I do load data from them.  For example, see this line in my file<a href=\"https://github.com/trulia/choroplethr/blob/master/R/county.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/trulia/choroplethr/blob/master/R/county.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792490087289000&amp;usg=AOvVaw184o7kZNY7XrNabmMjznIM\"> county.R</a></span></font></div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">  data(county.fips, package=&quot;maps&quot;, envir = environment())\r\n<br></span></font></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">So if someone does not have the maps package installed, it looks like installing my package will not install it for them, and then they get an error as soon as they hit this line.  </span></font></div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">So then the question becomes: how can I references this data in the NAMESPACE file so that R CMD CHECK is happy?  I tried to add this roxygen line:</span></font></div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><br></span></font></div><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">#&#39; @importFrom maps county.fips\r\n</span></font><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><br></span></font></div><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">But then my application fails to build with this error:</span></font></div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><br></span></font></div><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">** preparing package for lazy loading\r\nError : object ‘county.fips’ is not exported by &#39;namespace:maps&#39; </span></font><div style=\"padding-left:10px\"><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">ERROR: lazy loading failed for package ‘choroplethr’ </span></font></div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">And if you look at the NAMESPACE file for maps you can see that this is true.  </span></font></div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">Does anyone have advice on how to proceed? </span></font></div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">Thanks.  </span></font></div><div><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\"><br>\r\n\r\n</span></font></div><div><font face=\"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"white-space:normal\">Ari</span></font></div></div></pre></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;devtools&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">rdevtools+unsubscribe@<u></u>googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792490087289000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2smDuS7nqwzhwJUD2Xyx9_\">https://groups.google.com/<u></u>groups/opt_out</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div></div></div><br><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br>-- <br><a href=\"http://had.co.nz/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=